opkg-aiden
==========

Verbatim backport of Buildroot master's package/opkg (opkg 0.7.0) over the
opkg 0.4.5 recipe that ships in the vendored buildroot-2023.02.6 tarball.

Upstream provenance
-------------------

  Repository  https://gitlab.com/buildroot.org/buildroot
  Commit      073ea145df6e6c55427d6c8bf576622b5db19a53
              ("package/opkg: add optional libsolv dependency", 2024-12-29)
              -- the newest commit touching package/opkg as of 2026-07-30;
              master HEAD at backport time was
              9f17ac02b8561ca7adeb7911e4939b2ac9ad6320.
  Files       package/opkg/opkg.mk
              package/opkg/Config.in
              package/opkg/opkg.hash

  Backported byte-for-byte. Do NOT hand-edit OPKG_CONF_OPTS or
  OPKG_DEPENDENCIES: the upstream recipe already conditionalises every option
  on a Buildroot config symbol (libsolv, libcurl, openssl, zstd, xz, bzip2,
  lz4, gpg), so the recipe is driven entirely from the defconfig. Local
  divergence here is what caused repeated rework in earlier attempts.

  Refresh procedure: re-fetch the three files at a newer commit, update the
  SHAs above, and rebuild. Keep the COPYING hash line in opkg.hash -- Buildroot
  legal-info needs it.

Why an in-place overwrite instead of an out-of-tree package
-----------------------------------------------------------

buildroot-2023.02.6 already defines BR2_PACKAGE_OPKG and already registers
package/opkg/Config.in in package/Config.in, and opkg 0.7.0 is still autotools
(the release tarball ships a configure script). So the integration only needs
to replace three files -- unlike android-tools-aiden, no sed injection into
package/Config.in is required.

The buildroot tree is re-extracted from the tarball on every build
(sysdrv/Makefile), so the overwrite is re-applied by inject_opkg_aiden_pkg
from sync_buildroot_board_config after each extraction. Any *.patch file
dropped in this directory is copied into package/opkg/ as well, so
toolchain-compatibility patches (GCC 8 + uClibc-ng) can be added here without
touching the Makefile.

Enabled by these defconfig symbols
----------------------------------

  BR2_PACKAGE_OPKG=y      opkg itself (selects BR2_PACKAGE_LIBARCHIVE)
  BR2_PACKAGE_LIBSOLV=y   --with-libsolv; required by the download_first option
  BR2_PACKAGE_ZSTD=y      --enable-zstd

BR2_PACKAGE_OPENSSL, BR2_PACKAGE_LIBCURL and BR2_PACKAGE_XZ were already
enabled in luckfox_pico_w_defconfig and give --enable-curl / --enable-ssl-curl
/ --enable-xz for free.

BR2_PACKAGE_OPKG_GPG_SIGN is deliberately left off: no consumable signature
artefacts were found for the feeds this device can use, so enabling it would
pull in libgpgme + libgpg-error + gnupg with nothing to verify. See
docs/07-operations/opkg-package-management.md §3.6.

Runtime layout lives outside this directory: overlay/etc/init.d/S22opt,
overlay/etc/opkg/, overlay/etc/profile.d/aiden-opt.sh in the aiden repo.
